8% vs ~2.6% historically, with a 0.5-0.7 pass-through from g to r*: -0.35 pp.\n Delta r* = +0.35 +0.25 +0.15 -0.35 -0.10 -0.35 = -0.05 pp. NET-ZERO r*. This is the non-obvious result of the decomposition: demographic dissaving plus fiscal supply almost exactly cancel the growth, precaution and compression drags, so CQ4 is NOT an r* story.\nReal term premium: +0.40 pp of widening, from a current real 10y term premium of roughly +0.5 to +0.8. Drivers, all from the locked block: eroding sovereign convenience yields; levered hedge-fund basis-trade absorption means the marginal duration holder is a price-SENSITIVE leveraged account, not a price-insensitive reserve manager; 3-year P95 Debt-at-Risk 117% of GDP, +2.4pp more under a 20% AI-led equity shock; an equity-bond correlation that flips positive (duration that stops hedging must pay for itself); absent central-bank bid.\nFinancial-repression wedge: -0.20 pp = 0.35 probability of a material repression regime over 2032-36 (regulatory duration demand via LCR/Solvency-II/pension matching, YCC on the BoJ precedent, captive domestic buyers) x a -0.60pp average wedge when deployed.\nP50 = 1.82 - 0.05 + 0.40 - 0.20 = 1.97 -> 2.0%.\nBAND. P10 = 1.0%: regime D plus repression — an AI-capex-bust deflationary path with real yields crushed and Japan/euro reals pinned near zero. P90 = 3.3%: fiscal dominance with a term-premium spike, no repression, Japan normalizing, G7 reals above US TIPS' current level.\nSIM — REFUSAL AND DIRECTIONAL USE ONLY. The adapter states CQ4 is \"not identified\": capital.interestRate is an economy-wide REAL RETURN ON CAPITAL (an MPK), there is no 10y sovereign benchmark, no termPremium anywhere in src/, and no breakeven or inflation swap. I therefore take ZERO point estimate from it. Directional content I DO use, with the translation published: the model's economy-wide real rate averages 5.99-6.96% across scenarios and its debtRiskPremium averages 1.20-2.50pp, and the cross-scenario ORDERING is informative — tech-breakthrough gives the LOWEST risk premium (1.20pp) and debt-populism the HIGHEST (2.50pp, with the real rate at 6.96%), i.e. in a world where energy and automation capex compete for one financing pool, weak productivity plus fiscal stress widens premia. That ordering maps onto my CQ6-C/D split and supports an upper-half rather than lower-half CQ4, and it supports nothing else. Both readings are low-fertility-conditional.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:58.998Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"US median generator interconnection queue duration falls below 36 months (from ~60) in the LBNL \\\"Queued Up\\\" annual edition, AND quoted large-power-transformer lead times fall below 18 months per NEMA / Wood Mackenzie trade reporting.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2028\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My weakest-link identification is wrong: the physical build is not the 2036 cap. Raise CQ3 P50 from 1.8% to ~2.1% and P90 to ~3.0%; move ~8 points from B and D into CQ6-A (A 13 -> 21); raise the 2031-36 A-regime and B-regime returns on power/grid and construction by ~1.5 pp each; cut CQ5 by ~3.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"OECD-38 harmonized unemployment prints above 6.5% for two consecutive quarters WHILE OECD-38 job vacancies in ISIC Q (health and social work) remain above their 2025 level.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2029\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The mismatch channel dominates and my CQ1 conjunct-1 marginal of 0.55 is far too high. Cut CQ1 from 11 to ~5; cut CQ3 P50 by -0.2 pp to 1.6%; move ~10 points from CQ6-B into D (D 15 -> 25); cut healthcare-operator and ex-AI-equity returns in the B and D columns by ~1.5 pp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"China headline CPI 12-month average exceeds 2.0% in four consecutive quarters.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My highest-confidence leg (CQ2 conjunct B at 0